t like that grey steel tower!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Look at that beautiful blue glass wall!"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Colors </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Materials </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"red<br />grey<br />blue<br />brown<br />yellow\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"glass<br />metal<br />steel<br />wood<br />cement\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use a color and a material to talk about a building, you say the color first and the material second."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">A (1)blue (2)glass wall.</span><br />   color+material<br/><br/><span class = \"italic\">A (1)grey (2)steel building.</span><br/>  color+material<br/><br/>When there are two or more adjectives from the same group, we use the word <span class = \"strong\">and</span> between the two adjectives.  <br/><span class = \"italic\">Example: The boy has <span class = \"underline\">red</span> <span class = \"strong\">and</span> <span class = \"underline\">blue</span> hair!</span>"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Demonstrative Adjectives This and That"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A demonstrative adjective points out the noun it talks about. It goes before the noun."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This street is not the right one."}, {"type": "example", "content": "That building over there is the city hall."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">that</span> book                   &nbsp  &nbsp     &nbsp  &nbsp <span class=\"strong\">  this</span>  car"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">this</span> for something that is near."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You us <span class=\"strong\"> that</span> for something that is far."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to get back to "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "return to  a place again "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How do we get back to the bus station?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le09ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you are in a new city."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "brick "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a hard, heavy, rectangular block used to build walls and buildings. "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's a beautiful old red brick house."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le09ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wall "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the vertical structure that is part of a room "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She likes to paint the walls in her bedroom a light color."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le09ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "this way "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "this direction "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We have to go this way for the bus station."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le09ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tower "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a very tall building "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The office tower is all glass and metal."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le09ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name"